{#- The policy's permissions table, from the version's own `permissions` front matter. The same rows
    are published in `policy.json`, which a release compares with its build. On a phone each row
    stacks, its cells labelled from `data-label`. -#}
{#- It can still scroll sideways at an unusual width, so it takes focus. -#}
<section class="tablewrap" aria-label="Android permissions" tabindex="0">
<table class="permissions">
<thead><tr><th scope="col">Android permission</th><th scope="col">What it's for</th><th scope="col">If you say no</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
{% for p in permissions %}<tr><td data-label="Android permission"><code>{{ p.name }}</code></td><td data-label="What it's for">{{ p.for }}</td><td data-label="If you say no">{{ p.refused }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}</tbody>
</table>
</section>
